  "query_preview": "..(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 302 PM EDT SAT SEP 12 2026\n\nTo open the extended period, prominent features at 500 mb include a\ntrough over the Northeast, a ridge extending from the Upper Midwest\ndown through the Mississippi Valley, while a second trough is modeled\nover the Northern Rockies. The upper pattern remains fairly\nprogressive, with the ridge moving east over the Southeast US and Ohio\nValley by Tuesday, lasting through Wednesday. Thursday through\nSaturday, the second trough modeled over the Northern Rockies by\nMonday will slowly break the upper ridge down, ushering in cooler\nweather for Friday and Saturday.\n\nFor sensible weather, the new work week starts with a surface cold\nfront having just passed southeast of the area. Some lingering\nisolated showers remain possible early along the Virginia-Kentucky\nborder. Some residual river valley fog should mix out by mid-morning.\nTemperatures will be cooler, ranging from the upper 70s to mid 80s\nfrom north to south. A mix of sun and clouds can be expected early,\nbecoming fair in the afternoon and evening. With skies clearing out\nMonday night and high pressure building in, temperatures cool into the\nlow to mid 50s in the valleys, with upper 50s to low 60s along ridge\ntops. River valley fog is expected to develop again Monday night\nbefore mixing out Tuesday morning.\n\nWith the ridge shifting into the Southeast, high pressure builds into\nthe region, leading to temperatures warming into the upper 80s to low\n90s through Thursday. Shortwave energy associated with the second\ntrough brings shower and storm chances back to the CWA Thursday\nthrough Saturday. A cold front looks to progress into the forecast\narea from the Ohio Valley before stalling out Saturday. Agreement\namong model and ensemble guidance does widen heading towards the end\nof the week. With troughing energy seemingly breaking down the ridge\nheading into the weekend, high temperatures lax some, ranging from\nthe mid 80s to upper 80s north to south on Friday, and low 80s to\nmid 80s north to south on Saturday.",
